"content": "The so-called Nestor Ring was found in 1924 and was accepted as 
authentic by Sir Arthur Evans whereas many other scholars condemned it as a 
forgery. In recent years, scholars have claimed its authenticity anew. This 
article examines the background of the find circumstances and judges them 
suspicious. It also adds the criterion of semantic coherence in the debate and 
argues that the coherence depends on Egyptian prototypes and that the use of 
the butterfly motif argues against the artifact’s [...] the artifact’s 
